from pathlib import Path
p=Path('docs/PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md')
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
s=s.replace('# Smart Living production deployment guide','# Smart Living production deployment guide\n\n**Updated 16 October 2026:** use [PRODUCTION_LAUNCH.md](PRODUCTION_LAUNCH.md) as the current execution checklist. It covers the strict production profile, private document relocation, manifest assets, preflight, health probes and backup command. The detailed hosting/rollback reference below remains supplemental.')
s=s.replace('requirements-mysql.txt','requirements-production.txt')
s=s.replace('DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_A_UNIQUE_RANDOM_SECRET','DJANGO_ENV=production\nDJANGO_SECRET_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_A_UNIQUE_RANDOM_SECRET')
s=s.replace('**Production gates:** settings currently fall back to a development secret and `DEBUG=True` if not configured. A missing/misnamed `DJANGO_DB_ENGINE=mysql` also falls back to SQLite. Verify effective settings without printing passwords:', '**Production gates:** select `config.production` or set `DJANGO_ENV=production`. The production profile refuses missing/placeholder secrets, missing database values, SQLite fallback and unsafe hosts. Local development retains its separate defaults. Verify effective settings without printing passwords:')
s=s.replace('"DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE", "config.settings"','"DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE", "config.production"')
s=s.replace('Expect no normal system-check errors and no migration drift. Review every deployment warning. The current settings do not configure HSTS or `SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER`; do not promise a warning-free deployment. Enable HSTS through reviewed Django/web-server configuration only after HTTPS is reliable, starting with a short duration; do not include other subdomains or request preload without reviewing those domains.', 'Expect no normal system-check errors and no migration drift. Run `production_check --settings=config.production`. Production enables one-hour HSTS. W005/W021 are deliberately acknowledged because unreviewed child hosts and browser preload are not enabled; other deployment warnings fail the application preflight.')
s=s.replace("If TLS terminates at a reverse proxy, support must confirm how the original scheme reaches Django. Only set `SECURE_PROXY_SSL_HEADER = ('HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PROTO', 'https')` in reviewed application settings if the trusted proxy strips client-supplied values and sets the header itself. Adding a same-named `.env` variable alone has no effect: the current settings do not read it. Redirect loops must be resolved before public launch.", 'If TLS terminates at a reverse proxy, support must confirm that it strips client-supplied X-Forwarded-Proto and sets its own value. Only then set `DJANGO_TRUST_X_FORWARDED_PROTO=True`; the production profile reads this opt-in. Resolve redirect loops before launch.')
s=s.replace('This is an operator guide, not evidence of a live deployment.', 'Back up private documents as well as media and database; use the current `backup_site` command and restore procedure in PRODUCTION_LAUNCH.md. Product documents are now private on disk and downloaded through permission-checked /documents/ routes. Run secure_product_documents for files from older releases.\n\nThis is an operator guide, not evidence of a live deployment.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s += '''\n\n## Production release (cPanel / Passenger)\n\nUse [docs/PRODUCTION_LAUNCH.md](docs/PRODUCTION_LAUNCH.md). The strict `config.production` profile requires private credentials, exact hosts, MySQL and HTTPS; local `.env` settings remain for development. `scripts/init_production_env.py` generates an exclusive private template without displaying its secret. Install `requirements-production.txt`, migrate, relocate legacy document files, collect manifest static assets, and run `manage.py production_check --settings=config.production`.\n\nProduct documents are stored in private `var/private_documents` (or DJANGO_PRIVATE_DOCUMENT_ROOT) and served as checked attachments through `/documents/...`. They are included separately in `backup_site` backups. Transfer these private files separately from public media.\n\nBuild the allowlisted source ZIP with `python scripts/build_release.py`. Add `--include-catalogue` only when the offline seed assets are needed. Credentials, live records/media, private files and generated outputs are excluded. The old catalogue seed ZIP is not the production release.\n''';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
